<title>USA: Lucent says no cash payment involved with DSC.</title>
<headline>Lucent says no cash payment involved with DSC.</headline>
<dateline>MURRAY HILL, N.J. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lucent Technologies said Tuesday no cash payment or other agreement was involved in its settlemet with DSC Communications.</p>
<p>Lucent said DSC voluntarily dismissed its claims against Lucent and Lucent dismissed its counter-claim against DSC.</p>
<p>Earlier, Bell Atlantic and DSC settled their $1.6 billion anti-trust suit against Lucent, the clerk's office of the U.S. District Court said. Details of the settlement were not disclosed. Bell Atlantic sought $900 million and DSC $725.4 million in the suit accusing Lucent of controlling the telephone equipment market.</p>
</text>
